{meta title='Widgets'/}

<p>{tag 'widget'/} puts an interactive part on the page - tabs, an accordion, a carousel, a modal,
a dropdown, a toast and more, {echo php:count(padWidgetTypes())/} of them. Every one is built on
the server and works without JavaScript; where a widget has a script it only makes it handier,
and it is written once per page with the CSP nonce. Every widget is a file of
<code>pad/widgets/types/</code>, and the files there are the widgets there are.</p>

{example 'fragments/widgets_1'/}

<h2>Three ways to write one</h2>

<p>The tag names the widget, and its second parameter is the widget's own first:
<code>{open/}widget 'toast', 'Saved'/{close/}</code>. The widget: type does the same,
<code>{open/}widget:toast 'Saved'/{close/}</code>, and so does the bare name,
<code>{open/}toast 'Saved'/{close/}</code>. The bare name comes after every other kind of tag:
a store, a field or an array of the name wins, so a page's <code>$tabs</code> array is the data
of <code>{open/}tabs{close/}</code>.</p>

{example 'fragments/widgets_2'/}

<h2>What the browser does itself</h2>

<p>Each widget stands on what HTML and CSS can do: radio buttons and CSS for tabs and the wizard,
<code>&lt;details&gt;</code> for the accordion, a <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> for the modal, the
drawer and the toast, the <code>popover</code> attribute for the dropdown, <code>:hover</code>
and <code>:focus-within</code> for the tooltip, <code>:target</code> for the carousel's links and
the lightbox. The keyboard works because the browser's own controls are underneath; the scripts
add the arrow keys of a menu, Escape on a tooltip, the focus of a lightbox.</p>

{example 'fragments/widgets_3'/}

<h2>Items made by a loop</h2>

<p>Tabs, an accordion, a carousel, a wizard and a lightbox take {tag 'tab'/} items. A tab hands
its content to the nearest of them above it, so it may stand in an <code>{open/}if{close/}</code>
or in a loop over data - a step per row of a <code>{open/}data{close/}</code> store here.</p>

{example 'fragments/widgets_4'/}

<ul>
  <li>The colours are custom properties on <code>.pad-&lt;widget&gt;</code> -
  <code>--pad-tabs-accent</code>, <code>--pad-toast-success</code> and their like - with light
  and dark defaults.</li>
  <li><code>{open/}copy{close/}</code> stays a built-in tag that runs the copy widget, as PHP has
  a <code>copy()</code> function that a bare name would reach first; <code>{open/}tab{close/}</code>
  is a built-in tag too.</li>
  <li>A name that is no widget, an unknown option value and a widget without what it needs - a
  name, a label, a tab - are errors under the strict check.</li>
</ul>
